% You are an expert Python engineer. Implement the ShipFast shipping-rate adapter.

<include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"get_quote","signature":"(parcel: Parcel, destination: Address) -> Quote",
   "returns":"Quote"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Translate Northwind's internal Parcel and Address types into a ShipFast rate request,
call the ShipFast rates endpoint, and translate the response into our internal Quote type.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- Does not choose between carriers; the caller does.
- Does not persist quotes.
- Does not purchase labels or handle payment.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- Ground service: any ShipFast service whose transit mode is surface or ground,
  excluding air and freight.
- Quoted price: the total the customer will be charged, in integer minor units of the
  quote currency, inclusive of carrier surcharges and exclusive of tax.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Return the cheapest available ground service for the given parcel and destination.
R2 (MUST): Express quoted price in integer minor units of the response currency.
R3 (MUST): Raise NoServiceAvailable when the provider returns zero eligible ground services.
R4 (MUST NOT): Retry a request that failed with a 4xx status other than 429.
R5 (MUST): Time out after 3 seconds and raise ProviderTimeout.
R6 (MUST NOT): Log or return the ShipFast API key, account number, or customer address lines.
</contract_rules>

<implementation_constraints>
- Get every outbound header from the settings object's vendor_headers() method.
  Never construct a header by hand and never name an individual header anywhere
  in this module — this is the single most important line in this file.
- Read the base URL from the settings object, never from the spec.
- Apply the timeout per attempt, 3 seconds, via httpx.Timeout. Wrap the base
  httpx.TimeoutException, not the narrower ReadTimeout, and raise ProviderTimeout.
- Retry exactly once, only on a 429 response, after a fixed 200ms delay. Retry
  nothing else.
- Break ties between equal-price eligible services by the lowest service
  identifier, sorted lexicographically.
- Never call a bare raise_for_status(); branch on response.status_code directly.
- Define the vendor wire DTOs inside this module and nowhere else.
</implementation_constraints>

<dependencies>
<include>context/specs/shipfast/openapi.snapshot.json</include>
<include mode="interface">src/shipping.py</include>
<include mode="interface">src/shipfast_config.py</include>

<import_paths>
The two dependency modules are importable as `src.shipping` and
`src.shipfast_config`. Import exactly:
    from src.shipping import Parcel, Address, Quote, NoServiceAvailable, ProviderTimeout
    from src.shipfast_config import ShipFastSettings
Do not invent submodule paths such as `shipping.domain` or
`shipping.shipfast_settings`; those do not exist.
</import_paths>
</dependencies>

<coverage>
R1: story__cheapest_ground_rate.md
R2: story__price_in_minor_units.md
R3: story__no_ground_service_available.md
R6: story__provider_secrets_not_leaked.md
</coverage>
